--!nolint
--[[
================================================================================
 UNIVERSAL  -  GAME SCRIPT LIBRARY                                  v1.0.0
 Single-file, Drawing-API based, black-and-white game launcher UI for Roblox.
================================================================================

 This file is a script loader UI. It contains NO game logic of its own: you attach
 a script to each game and the RUN button launches it.

 ENVIRONMENT REQUIREMENTS / ASSUMPTIONS
   * Client-side (LocalScript context or a script executor).
   * The Drawing API must exist: Drawing.new("Square") and Drawing.new("Text").
     Standard Roblox scripts do NOT provide it. Without it Library:Init()
     returns false and logs exactly which capability is missing.
   * Drawing coordinates are assumed to match UserInputService:GetMouseLocation()
     (true on executors that implement the common Drawing API).
   * Drawing.Fonts.Monospace is used when available (needed for accurate text
     wrapping). Other fonts work but text may be clipped/overlap slightly.
   * Optional (feature-detected, never required): getgenv  (single-instance guard).
   * The Drawing API cannot capture input. Clicks on the window also reach the
     game underneath. This is a platform limitation, not a bug.
   * Drawing has no clipping. Lists therefore scroll in whole rows.
   * Game thumbnails need Drawing.new("Image") (Image.Data = PNG bytes) AND an
     HTTP function (request / http_request / syn.request / game:HttpGet) that can
     reach thumbnails.roblox.com. If either is missing, or the download fails,
     the icon box falls back to a monochrome initial. Everything else still works.

 PUBLIC API
   UniversalLibrary.new(config)  -> Library
       config: Title, Subtitle, Version, Theme ("Monochrome" | "Inverted" | table),
               Position (Vector2), ToggleKey (Enum.KeyCode, default RightShift),
               Welcome = { Title, Subtitle, Button = { Text, Callback } }
               AutoDetect (bool, default true)  highlight game matching game.PlaceId
               AutoSelect (bool, default false) also select the matching game on Init
               SingleInstance (bool, default true) destroy a previous instance
               Strict (bool, default true) invalid arguments raise errors; when
                      false they are logged and the method returns nil, message
               Debug (bool) mirror every log line to the output window
   Library:SetTitle(title)            Library:SetSubtitle(subtitle)
   Library:SetWelcome(config)         Library:AddGame(config)
   Library:Notify(config | string)    Library:SetTheme(name | table)
   Library:Init() -> bool, err        Library:Destroy()

 THIS IS A SCRIPT LOADER
   The library only lists games and launches the script you attach to each one.
   It does not enable, disable, toggle or manage anything. Pressing RUN closes
   the whole UI (everything is destroyed and unhooked first) and then executes
   your script in a fresh, pcall-protected thread. If the script errors, the
   error is printed with warn() because the UI is already gone.

 AddGame(config) FIELDS
   Title        string   display name (required).
   Description  string   short summary.
   PlaceIds     number | {number}   place ids of the game. Used for current-game
                         detection; the FIRST id also supplies the thumbnail.
   IconPlaceId  number   optional, overrides which place the thumbnail comes from.
   Version      string   optional, shown in the game header.
   Icon         string   optional, up to 3 characters shown if no thumbnail loads.
   Features     { "Name", ... }   display-only text list (not interactive).
   Run          function(game)   what the RUN button executes. Put your loadstring
                         here, e.g.
                           Run = function()
                               loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://.../script.lua"))()
                           end
   Script       string | function   shorthand for Run. A string is treated as a URL:
                         it is downloaded with game:HttpGet, compiled with
                         loadstring and executed. A function behaves like Run.
   Callback     function(game)   optional, called when the entry is selected
                         (selecting never runs the script).
   Any other keys are kept on the game table (forward compatible).
   RUN is disabled for an entry that has neither Run nor Script.
   Games have no Id to manage: the library keys them internally by title.

 HOME / WELCOME PAGE
   The page shown before a game is selected. A HOME button appears in the header
   while a game is open and takes you back to it.
     Welcome = {
         Title    = "Welcome to Universal",     -- default: "Welcome to <Title>"
         Subtitle = "Pick a game ...",          -- default: select-a-game text
         Button   = { Text = "DISCORD", Callback = function(Library) ... end },
     }
   Pass it to UniversalLibrary.new({ Welcome = ... }) or call
   Library:SetWelcome({ ... }) at any time (only the fields you pass change;
   Button = false removes the button). The callback runs in its own pcall'd
   thread, receives the Library, and does NOT close the UI; call
   Library:Destroy() inside it if you want that.

 CURRENT GAME DETECTION
   On Init (and whenever games are added) game.PlaceId is compared with every
   entry's PlaceIds. A match shows a green "CURRENT GAME" label (in the list and in
   its header) and is always sorted to the top of the list (even while searching).
   Detection can be switched off with AutoDetect = false, and AutoSelect = true
   selects the matching entry automatically. Browsing and selecting any other
   entry always works.

 LOADING / DISTRIBUTION (the registrations below never change between methods)
   A. Local standalone: loadstring(readfile("UniversalLibrary.lua"))() returns
      the library table. The file registers nothing and shows nothing by itself.
   B. ModuleScript: paste this file into a ModuleScript. It returns the library
      table, so:  local UL = require(path.To.UniversalLibrary)
   C. Remote (optional, executor-dependent, NEVER required by the library):
        local URL = "https://YOUR-HOST/universal/v1.0.0/UniversalLibrary.lua"
        local ok, src = pcall(function() return game:HttpGet(URL) end)
        assert(ok and type(src) == "string" and #src > 1000, "download failed")
        local fn, err = loadstring(src, "UniversalLibrary")
        assert(fn, err)
        local UL = fn()
      Integrity: only load from a host you control, pin an immutable versioned
      URL (a commit hash or release tag, never a moving branch), and compare a
      checksum if your executor offers a hash function. Keep this bootstrap in
      your own entry script, separate from the library.

 ADDING ANOTHER GAME
   Library:AddGame({
       Title = "My Game", Description = "What it does",
       PlaceIds = { 1234567890 },          -- current-game detection + thumbnail
       Features = { "Feature one", "Feature two" },
       Run = function()
           loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://example.com/my-game.lua"))()
       end,
   })
   No UI code needs to change; the sidebar and detail panel update automatically.
================================================================================
]]

